# Source of truth
Read `docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, the current milestone in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, and `docs/STATUS.md`. When they conflict, stop and record the conflict rather than guessing.

# Scope discipline
- Implement one milestone or one narrowly stated task only.
- Do not add speculative abstractions for future milestones.
- Do not replace the selected stack without an ADR.
- Keep offline child flow independent from Laravel.

# Architecture
- Vue SPA; no Inertia or SSR.
- Domain logic belongs in framework-independent TypeScript packages.
- Vue components do not import Tauri APIs or persistence libraries directly.
- Use ports/adapters for input, storage, export, audio, sharing and synchronization.
- Persist logical Unicode text, never Arabic presentation-form code points.
- Treat camera light tracking as a separate `InputAdapter`, not as Pointer Events.

# Quality
- TypeScript strict mode; no unexplained `any`.
- PHP strict types and small action/service classes.
- Add behavior-focused tests with each change.
- Run targeted tests, typecheck and lint before finishing.
- Never weaken tests or coverage thresholds to make a task pass.
- Keep migrations reversible and API changes documented.

# Privacy and security
- Local-only is the default.
- Never upload data without an explicit eligible consent snapshot.
- Do not persist raw camera frames by default.
- OTP codes are hashed, short-lived, single-use, rate-limited and attempt-limited.
- Check authorization on every admin operation.

# Token efficiency
- Inspect only relevant files.
- State the intended file changes briefly before editing.
- Avoid large generated output in chat; write files directly.
- Reuse fixtures and shared contracts.
- Finish by updating `docs/STATUS.md` with completed criteria and the next smallest task.
